Z||000000||Fiero Justin||03-04-2001||07:46 AM||||Does anyone know how to adjust the backup light switch on an 86 SE with the 4 speed.  I need this help quick, seeing I got pulled over for the Reverse lights coming on when down shifting.||||reg||4
Z||000001||TheFiero64||03-04-2001||10:14 AM||||On the 4 speed it is in the center console near the shifter. There are 2 6mm screws under each ash tray to remove the console. Just look for a switch. I don't know if it can be adjusted, but look to see what it is doing.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||03-04-2001||10:47 AM||||On my 86SE therre is a little screw on hte end of the switch  for adjustment also the mount for the switch may be bent??<P>I'm with Josh, Take a look down there and see if it looks ok? may need some to look at the lights when you shift!<P>There's more info. Do a search, use "Back up lights" search word.<P>Here's one: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007803.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007803.html</A> <P>DXR_DAD<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 03-04-2001).]||||reg||1
